        "title": "ADMISSION SUMMARY",
        "content": "Dear Doctor,\n Thank you for your ongoing care of [], a []-year-old [] who presented to the [] at [] on [] with <CIT id=\"c1\">4-week history of cough</CIT>.\n The primary diagnosis was <CIT id=\"c2\">mild Community Acquired Pneumonia (CAP)</CIT>. Key symptoms included <CIT id=\"c3\">ongoing cough for 4 weeks</CIT>, which <CIT id=\"c4\">worsened in the past 5 days with more productive green phlegm</CIT>, <CIT id=\"c5\">chest pain secondary to cough</CIT> described as \"burning\", and <CIT id=\"c6\">pre-syncopal and dyspnoeic yesterday after exertion</CIT>. The patient also reported <CIT id=\"c7\">worsened anxiety</CIT> with ongoing symptoms. Relevant past medical history includes <CIT id=\"c18\">Asthma</CIT>, <CIT id=\"c19\">Anxiety</CIT>, and <CIT id=\"c20\">Depression</CIT>, with current medications being <CIT id=\"c21\">Propanolol 10mg daily</CIT> and <CIT id=\"c22\">Escitalopram 20mg daily</CIT>. On examination, the patient <CIT id=\"c8\">appeared well</CIT> and was <CIT id=\"c9\">conversing comfortably with no respiratory distress</CIT>, but was <CIT id=\"c10\">tachycardic</CIT> with <CIT id=\"c11\">cough exacerbated by deep breathing</CIT> and <CIT id=\"c12\">?right lower inspiratory creps</CIT>. Investigations including <CIT id=\"c13\">bloods</CIT>, <CIT id=\"c14\">CXR</CIT>, and <CIT id=\"c15\">ECG</CIT> were planned. Treatment involved <CIT id=\"c16\">analgesia</CIT> and the patient was deemed suitable for discharge with <CIT id=\"c17\">oral antibiotics</CIT>.",
